// The Sense/Net deck's sound pack: a friendly consumer machine. Simple square beeps, a warm
// chord for good news (the startup-chime family), and a gentle "boing" when something goes wrong.
// Same format as ono.ron (see there); every cue needs an entry.
//
// Music: a 1980s Mac adventure or learning game. Square tunes over triangle basses, in major
// keys at a walking pace, with a countermelody that drops out when the trace runs high and only
// a soft shaker for drums. Each tier keeps its chords on a 4- or 8-bar cycle, so tracks of
// different lengths drift against each other without clashing.
(
    cues: [
        (cue: Hop,      notes: [(wave: Square,   from: 1320, to: 1320, ms: 18,  vol: 0.10)]),
        (cue: IceRez,   notes: [(wave: Square,   from: 880,  to: 880,  ms: 60,  vol: 0.16),
                                (wave: Square,   from: 660,  to: 660,  ms: 90,  vol: 0.16)]),
